  "title": "BNCI 2014-002 Motor Imagery dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 14 healthy participants performing two-class motor imagery (right hand versus feet) in a cue-guided Graz-BCI paradigm with continuous visual feedback. Each participant completed a single session of 8 runs and 160 trials, recorded at 512 Hz from 15 Laplacian-derived EEG channels. The dataset supports benchmarking of classifiers such as random forests and shrinkage LDA for sensorimotor rhythm brain-computer interfaces.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with g.USBamp amplifiers and active Ag/AgCl electrodes (g.LADYbird cap) at 512 Hz, referenced to the left mastoid and grounded at the right mastoid, using BCI2000. Data were online filtered with 8th-order Butterworth band-pass filters. Each session comprised recording, training and feedback phases with 80 trials each of right-hand and feet motor imagery, 5 s per trial.",
